From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: raphael1688 <schuey@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 08 Nov 2026 08:18:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Patch add API tokens to the user menu

A token from logging in lasts one day, which makes scripts log in on
every run. Add "API Tokens" to the user menu: confirm your password
(and two-factor code, when enabled), pick a lifetime from 1 day to
3 years, and get a token that is shown once with a copy button.

  - POST /tokens and POST /tokens/2fa take an optional expiry, limited
    to 1d, 7d, 30d, 90d, 1y, 2y and 3y. Without one, logins still get
    the default day, so the login page is unchanged.

  - GET /tokens no longer honours ?expiry=. It let any session token be
    swapped for one of any length without the password, which would
    make the password check above pointless. Nothing in the app sent
    it; a refresh now always lasts the default day.

  - Tokens are not stored, so there is no list to revoke from. The
    existing per-request checks still apply: changing the password
    ends every token issued before it, and disabling or deleting the
    user ends all of its tokens.

  - It lives in the user menu rather than Settings because Settings is
    admin only, while the advice is to give scripts a dedicated user
    with only the permissions they need.

  - The Clipboard API is missing on plain http origins, which is how
    the admin port is usually reached, so copying falls back to the
    selection.
